{% doc %}
  Answers the MCP engine's question "must this proposed change wait for a
  person?" from the desk's own settings, so support admins decide it in the desk
  rather than someone editing an instance constant.

  Two settings, in this order:

  - `mcp_require_approval` — the desk-wide switch. Missing means ON, so a desk
    that has never thought about this gets the safe answer. An explicit false
    turns approval off for every tool.
  - `mcp_approval_exempt_tools` — the names of tools that go straight through
    while the desk-wide switch is on. It names exemptions rather than the tools
    that need approval, so a tool added to the desk later is gated until an
    admin says otherwise.

  Comparison is an exact match on the tool name, never a substring: `contains`
  on a setting that somehow held a string would match a prefix, and the wrong
  answer here runs something nobody agreed to.

  The engine reads `enforced` on every call (queries/approval/enforced), so a
  change takes effect on the next request. `desk_switch` and `exempt` are the
  raw settings, for the Assistants panel to draw its toggles from: a tool's own
  toggle shows its own setting, not what the desk-wide switch currently makes of
  it.

  @param {string} [tool_name] - the tool the engine is about to run. Without it
    only the desk-wide switch is consulted: an unnamed tool is never exempt.
  @return {object} { enforced, desk_switch, exempt }
{% enddoc %}
{% liquid
  function settings = 'modules/support/helpers/settings'

  assign desk_switch = true
  if settings.mcp_require_approval == false
    assign desk_switch = false
  endif

  assign exempt = settings.mcp_approval_exempt_tools
  if exempt == blank
    assign exempt = []
  endif

  assign out = { "enforced": true }
  assign out['desk_switch'] = desk_switch
  assign out['exempt'] = exempt

  unless desk_switch
    assign out['enforced'] = false
    return out
  endunless

  unless tool_name == blank
    for exempt_name in exempt
      if exempt_name == tool_name
        assign out['enforced'] = false
      endif
    endfor
  endunless
  return out
%}
